# Kotlin SDUI engine

- Keep the engine in `sdui/` (`model`, `registry`, `runtime`, `mvi`, `render`). Screens in `ui/`. Shared leaves live in `ui/components/` and are used by both the SDUI renderer and the static home twin.
- **MVI only.** View emits `SduiIntent`. `SduiReducer` is a pure function. `SduiViewModel` holds `StateFlow<SduiUiState>` and one-shot `SduiEffect`. Do not add `mutableStateOf` controllers or page-specific ViewModel fields (`tenureMonths`).
- Parse with `kotlinx.serialization`. Single `SduiNode` / `SduiAction` with `type: String` — not sealed per-widget subtypes.
- Registry maps `type` → composable. Unknown type → fallback. No giant `when` in `MainActivity`.
- Leaves call `scope.dispatch(actions)` → `SduiIntent.ExecuteNodeActions`. Bindings read `scope.nodeState`.
- Images load with Coil. Measure parse vs compose separately for `PERF.md`.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — mutable controller / page fields
class SduiController { var tenureMonths by mutableStateOf(24) }

// ✅ GOOD
viewModel.onIntent(SduiIntent.ExecuteNodeActions(node.actions))
```
